{
  "idea_units": [
    {
      "line_start": 70,
      "line_end": 72,
      "text": "An LLM can process a text chunk containing multiple objects/ideas simultaneously. It will identify and store all of them, so there is no need to worry about truncation causing data loss or to strictly feed it one object at a time.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 73,
      "line_end": 78,
      "text": "A distinction was made between two transcript processing strategies: a \"top-down\" approach where the LLM segments a large chunk of text, and a \"bottom-up\" approach where the LLM labels and merges smaller, pre-defined units. The discussion favored exploring a bottom-up method.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 79,
      "line_end": 80,
      "text": "Existing bottom-up methods have significant drawbacks: using fixed-size chunks (e.g., every 3 turns) can incorrectly merge multiple ideas, while processing sentence-by-sentence is computationally very expensive.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 80,
      "line_end": 82,
      "text": "A new \"dynamic chunking\" method was proposed as a compromise. This method would read a sentence and forecast how many subsequent turns are on the same topic, grouping them into a variable-length block for the LLM to process.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 83,
      "line_end": 89,
      "text": "The evaluation plan for the dynamic chunking method involves comparing it against fixed-chunk methods (both N-turn and turn-by-turn) to analyze the trade-offs.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 88,
      "line_end": 89,
      "text": "Key evaluation metrics will be the number of LLM requests (as a proxy for computational cost) and the quality of the generated output compared to other methods.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 90,
      "line_end": 91,
      "text": "A formal evaluation framework using precision and recall against a human-annotated set of important idea units was suggested to measure performance.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 91,
      "line_end": 92,
      "text": "The hypothesis is that the dynamic method will achieve high precision and high recall, capturing important ideas without including noise or losing information. This research could become a resource on efficient meeting information processing.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    }
  ]
}

