    {
      "line_start": 146,
      "line_end": 147,
      "text": "A key trade-off of the top-down approach is its unpredictability. When given a large chunk of text, the number of topics the LLM identifies is variable and depends entirely on the model's discretion.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 148,
      "line_end": 149,
      "text": "The discussion shifts to exploring 'bottom-up' methods. One variant described is to segment the transcript into fixed-size chunks (e.g., every three turns), generate a small summary for each, and then iteratively combine these into a higher-level summary.",
