{
  "idea_units": [
    {
      "line_start": 154,
      "line_end": 156,
      "text": "An experiment is proposed to compare a dynamic transcript chunking method against a fixed-size chunking method (e.g., fixed number of turns like 3 or 5) to show the trade-offs.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 158,
      "line_end": 159,
      "text": "A primary metric for comparison will be the number of computations (API requests). For example, if a dynamic method creates 20 chunks from 100 turns, it can be compared to a fixed method with a chunk size of 5.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 160,
      "line_end": 160,
      "text": "A key difference between the methods is that dynamic chunking creates variable-length segments based on topic, whereas fixed chunking creates segments of uniform turn count.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 161,
      "line_end": 161,
      "text": "An alternative, highly granular method to compare against is creating a summary for every single turn and then merging them. This is expected to be computationally expensive and capture many unimportant items.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 162,
      "line_end": 162,
      "text": "The dynamic method's implementation involves having the model forecast, based on the current turn, how many subsequent turns will cover the same topic to determine the chunk boundary. This is perceived as simple to implement.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 165,
      "line_end": 166,
      "text": "The quality of the output can be evaluated using precision and recall against a human-defined set of important idea units.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 166,
      "line_end": 167,
      "text": "It is hypothesized that the iterative per-turn summary method would have high recall but low precision, while the proposed dynamic method could achieve both high precision and high recall.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 165,
      "line_end": 169,
      "text": "The overall goal is to develop a method that reduces computation while increasing the fineness of information extraction from meetings, which could be a direct research result.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    }
  ]
}

