{
  "idea_units": [
    {
      "line_start": 197,
      "line_end": 198,
      "text": "There is a concern about the lack of control with the current single-prompt approach. It is proposed to break down the task into smaller, sequential steps, each with its own prompt, to make the process easier to check.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 198,
      "line_end": 198,
      "text": "An example of a multi-step process is to first have the model judge if a topic is large or small and estimate the number of related sentences before proceeding.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 200,
      "line_end": 201,
      "text": "The current method is criticized as a black box that executes the entire task at once, making it impossible to check, control, or adjust intermediate steps.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 202,
      "line_end": 202,
      "text": "An alternative is to use programmatic control, where external code tracks which sentences have been processed (e.g., with a boolean variable) and then calls the model for each new step, rather than having the model manage the entire sequence internally.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 203,
      "line_end": 206,
      "text": "There is a discussion about whether step-wise control is possible with the current setup. One speaker believes it is, while the other argues that the prompt must be broken into separate parts to allow for intervention between steps.",
      "completeness": "incomplete",
      "uncertainty_note": "The speakers are trying to clarify what the other means and have not reached a conclusion."
    },
    {
      "line_start": 209,
      "line_end": 209,
      "text": "A concrete failure of the current autonomous method is cited as evidence: after processing lines 1-40, the model incorrectly started the next segment from line 31.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 209,
      "line_end": 209,
      "text": "This failure also highlights a lack of observability, as it was impossible to know how many idea units the model had identified within the 1-40 lines or what its internal state was.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    }
  ]
}

