{
  "idea_units": [
    {
      "line_start": 338,
      "line_end": 339,
      "text": "The current process can be modified into a manager-based architecture where tool calls return not just an output, but also a prompt, allowing the manager to iterate in a way that mimics a multi-agent system.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 340,
      "line_end": 340,
      "text": "A key advantage of a multi-agent architecture is that each agent can be individually tuned and tested, making it easier to see how a change to one agent affects its specific output.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 341,
      "line_end": 342,
      "text": "In the current monolithic process, the effects of each step are compounded, making it difficult to debug and pinpoint the source of an error, such as poor idea unit splitting.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 343,
      "line_end": 345,
      "text": "A counter-argument is that if the system could output a complete log of its tool-calling process—including which tool was called, why, and the result—it would provide enough transparency to understand its behavior, similar to a multi-agent system.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 345,
      "line_end": 346,
      "text": "The current tool-calling mechanism is argued to be like a multi-agent system because it can send multiple requests to Gemini in one call and receive separate results for each, handling them in a single request-response cycle.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 346,
      "line_end": 347,
      "text": "The prompts for each step in the current process are separate and can be modified. By analyzing logs, one can see the model's step-by-step decisions and adjust prompts accordingly.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 347,
      "line_end": 347,
      "text": "The speaker's concluding opinion is that important tasks should be separated into distinct agents for processing.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    }
  ]
}

